its session’s identifier. A session goes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"te